    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 270 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `displayName` field on the owner response, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field (getter/setter/`@JsonProperty`).\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getDisplayName()` method returning `lastName + \", \" + firstName`. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`: `ownerDto.setDisplayName(owner.getDisplayName())`), so it's returned on create and every other owner response.\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to assert `$.displayName` equals `\"Washington, George\"`.\n\nThe compute happens through the entity getter and MapStruct, so no controller changes were needed \u2014 the create endpoint (and all owner responses) now include the field.",
